Independent runtime verification: migration validation

Invocation:
  npm run migrate:validate

Observed:
  PASS — 103 files; sequence contiguous 00001..00103; no convention errors.
  The repository validator reported 35 data-insert warnings and exited
  successfully.

Invocation:
  VALIDATE_STRICT=1 bash scripts/validate-migrations.sh

Observed:
  FAIL — strict mode promoted the same 35 historical data-insert warnings to
  errors. The findings are in migrations 00004, 00008, 00028, 00061, 00075,
  00079, 00087, 00092, 00093, and 00096; no 00103-specific lint error was
  reported.

Direct migration evidence:
  00103_legacy_conflict_materialization.sql contains a multi-statement
  dollar-quoted PL/pgSQL function at lines 14-31 without Goose
  StatementBegin/StatementEnd markers. The integration runner therefore
  splits the function at its first semicolon and PostgreSQL rejects it.
